2.1 Stage-1: Radiographic Input Validator (xray_validator.keras)
Problem Addressed: Previous iterations accepted arbitrary images (selfies, documents, pet photos, intraoral camera snapshots) and produced misleading pathology classifications.
Solution: Trained and deployed a MobileNetV2 binary classification model specifically on a curated corpus of authentic panoramic radiographs (OPGs) against non-dental distractor images.
Fail-Safe Gate: If Stage 1 confidence is $< 0.50$, inference is immediately halted with valid_xray: false, and no Grad-CAM or pathology assessment is executed.
2.2 Stage-2: Multi-Class Pathology Classifier (smileguard_model.keras)
Architecture: EfficientNetB0 backbone with customized top pooling, dense dropout ($p = 0.3$), and dense classification head.
Target Pathologies:
0: Dental Caries (Enamel/dentin radiolucencies)
1: Impacted Teeth (Third molar impactions, ectopic eruptions)
2: Periapical Lesions (Apical granulomas, periapical abscesses)
3: Periodontal Bone Loss (Horizontal/vertical alveolar crest resorption)
Softmax Probability Vector: Dynamically computes true probabilities where $\sum_{i=1}^4 P(C_i) = 1.0$.
2.3 Mathematical Pre-Softmax Grad-CAM (gradcam.py)
Saturation Prevention: Gradients $\frac{\partial y^c}{\partial A^k}$ are calculated against the linear pre-softmax logit $y^c$ for the predicted class rather than post-softmax probabilities (which suffer from gradient vanishing on high-confidence inputs).
Target Feature Layer: top_activation ($7 \times 7 \times 1280$ activation volume).
Heatmap Rendering: Normalized with OpenCV COLORMAP_JET and alpha-blended ($\alpha = 0.40$) directly over the original radiograph.
